          <h3 class="journal-card-title" style="margin-top:1rem;">Chester — The Burh Æthelflæd Defended with Bees</h3>
          <p class="journal-card-excerpt">Chester was refounded as a burh in 907 AD. When a Viking raiding party attacked shortly after, the Chronicle records an extraordinary defence — townswomen pouring boiling ale from the walls, and, in some accounts, hives of bees thrown at the attackers.</p>
